es _mutation_to_batch_dict' — but they are structurally different and select different mutation sets. An empty local_fields still populates `changed` from jira-side values (differ.py:579-597, where local_val=None != jira_val), so condition (A) suppresses payloads that condition (B) would keep. The plan must pick the ONE condition that matches its own definition of 'inert' (empty EFFECTIVE payload) rather than offering a false equivalence.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8cd2274685f52729","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section","norm_id":"nb4476db8c235d1d6","priority":0.67,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A key present in both with empty local_fields but non-trivial jira drift — (A) skips it, (B) emits it."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Restate AC4 with a concrete cardinality assertion, e.g. 'rev-parse invocations on a converged key-set pass == 0 (or baseline minus ~516)', tied to the same corpus fixture as AC1/AC3.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["F1","E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1875,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'git rev-parse invocation count per pass drops correspondingly'","E6 verify-taxonomy item (5): missing cardinality assertion when the criterion names a count","The Why section quantifies the expectation ('~516 extra git invocations per pass') so a concrete before/after target is available"],"finding":"AC4 asserts git rev-parse invocations 'drop correspondingly' but states no concrete target count, so a counting-shim integration test has no numeric assertion to check against.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbb54f3ee0d55ffa8","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, line 4 ('git rev-parse invocation count per pass drops correspondingly')","norm_id":"na5c71d1ca64d96a1","priority":0.4125,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer writes a shim that observes any decrease and passes, even if only a fraction of the inert mutations were skipped"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Change AC4 to: 'On the converged key-set pass, git rev-parse invocation count drops from N to N-516 (assert the delta equals the count of skipped inert mutations via the counting shim).'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"lo